# Purpose
Design is web-first; ensure the app also fits well on mobile: works on phones and tablets, responsive layouts, and good UX on small screens.

## Do / Don't

### DO
DO use web-first layouts (desktop as primary), then ensure they scale down well: test from 320px up; use min-width media queries when adapting for smaller viewports.
DO include viewport: in Next.js use `export const viewport = { width: 'device-width', initialScale: 1 }` in `app/layout.tsx`, or the `viewport` export in metadata.
DO use flexible layouts: CSS Grid and Flexbox; avoid fixed widths for containers.
DO ensure touch targets (buttons, links, form controls) are ≥ 44×44px.
DO avoid horizontal scroll on small screens; constrain images and tables.
DO test on real devices or browser DevTools device emulation (iPhone SE, Android, tablet).

### DON'T
MUST NOT use `user-scalable=no` or `maximum-scale=1` unless absolutely required (accessibility).
MUST NOT rely on hover-only interactions; provide tap/click alternatives for touch.
MUST NOT use fixed positioning that obscures content on small screens without safe-area consideration.

## Breakpoints
| Name | Min width | Typical use |
|------|-----------|-------------|
| sm   | 640px     | Large phone / small tablet |
| md   | 768px     | Tablet |
| lg   | 1024px    | Desktop |
| xl   | 1280px    | Large desktop |

## Completion Checklist
[ ] Viewport configured in app/layout.tsx (viewport export or metadata).
[ ] No horizontal overflow at 320px width.
[ ] Touch targets ≥ 44×44px.
[ ] Layout tested at 375px, 768px, 1024px.
